\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 Verilog Four-Valued Logic\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf0 \
0 (Logic Zero) - In Physical World\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 Logic Zero:
\f2\b0  Represents boolean "false" or the result of negation (~a).\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 Strong Zero:
\f2\b0  Corresponds to a physical ground (GND/0V) connection.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 False Case:
\f2\b0  Defines the "false" condition in conditional logic like if statements.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 Low State:
\f2\b0  Indicates the lower voltage threshold in a digital signal range.\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 \
1 (Logic One) - In Physical World\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 Logic One:
\f2\b0  Represents boolean "true" or a logical assertion (a).\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 Strong One:
\f2\b0  Corresponds to a physical supply voltage V
\fs16 CC 
\fs26 or V
\fs16 DD
\fs26  connection.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 True Case:
\f2\b0  Defines the "true" condition in conditional logic.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 High State:
\f2\b0  Indicates the upper voltage threshold in a digital signal range.\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 \
X (Unknown / Don't Care) - Only in Simulation\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 Unknown:
\f2\b0  A signal state that cannot be determined during simulation.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 Conflict:
\f2\b0  Occurs when two competing drivers (0 and 1) drive the same net, resulting in an indeterminate value.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 Metastability:
\f2\b0  A condition where a signal violates setup/hold timing, causing the output to hover between 0 and 1.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 Uninitialized:
\f2\b0  The default state for registers/memory upon simulation startup before valid data is clocked in.\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 \
Z (High Impedance / Floating) - In Physical World\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 Disconnected:
\f2\b0  No active driver exists; the node behaves as an open circuit.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 Tri-state Logic:
\f2\b0  Essential for bus architectures where a device must electrically "disconnect" from a shared bus.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 High Impedance:
\f2\b0  Provides near-infinite resistance, making the signal highly susceptible to ambient electrical noise.\
}